id: pm-5iwfkj
title: "GH-1354: Linked-test snapshot mode drops nested package dependencies and breaks monorepo acceptance"
description: Published linked-test snapshot mode reportedly loses independently installed nested package dependencies.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,context-management,github-intake
created_at: "2026-09-30T06:48:35.183Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T00:12:20.823Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-03T00:12:20.030Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-03T00:12:20.030Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Real filesystem regression retains distinct root and nested dependency versions without flattening; Snapshot and ordinary linked runs preserve PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH isolation; Dependency write/isolation behavior is documented and tested; Current built and packed artifacts pass the reporter contract
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Preserve root and nested installations and their alias namespaces independently of copy order, including external and linked packages; rebase ordinary physical source aliases, retain missing suffixes, reject reserved/unadmitted targets and overlapping physical destinations before copying."
expected_result: Each admitted dependency namespace keeps its original resolution behavior while source writes remain disposable and physical destination overlap produces an actionable refusal without changing original bytes.
actual_result: "Ten owner-linked real filesystem/CLI cases pass in test-local-murm7irm-iqatr0. Shared canonical test-local-murmvdoi-pilgng passes 9629 tests, and measured test-local-murmxdfi-0nvqus records exact 100/100/100/100 with the complete source denominator. Real temporary npm installations and aliases work under both Node and Bun CLI backends and linked commands; original bytes remain intact. Static, four-project typecheck, packed consumers and 89-command dogfood pass. Native Windows passed 4017735; the final pushed revision will receive renewed required checks and provider reviews before merge."
